winewayland: keep the toplevel state when a configure has no toplevel event

An xdg_surface.configure ends a configure sequence. The sequence need not
contain an xdg_toplevel.configure: the size and states of the toplevel then
stay as they were. The driver cleared its pending toplevel state after every
sequence, so such a sequence was read as "no size, no states", which for a
maximized window is a request to leave the maximized state.
Hyprland 0.56.2 sends one whenever a window becomes hidden or visible again:
it wants to change the suspended state, which exists from xdg_wm_base
version 6, and for an older client it only schedules the surface configure
(XDGShell.cpp, setSuspeneded). The driver binds version 2. Every switch away
from the workspace of a Wine window therefore cleared WS_MAXIMIZE, and a
WinForms form answered by going back to its restored size inside a tile that
kept its size. The next toplevel configure, usually sent when the window is
focused again, put it right; a window shown again without the focus stayed
at the wrong size.
Keep the size and states of the last xdg_toplevel.configure for the next
sequence. A compositor that supports the suspended state sends the same
values again in that situation.
Applies after wine-11.18-wayland-parent.patch. Wine master had the same code
on 2026-11-18.
Wine-derived change: LGPL-2.1-or-later.

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
@@ -58,7 +58,12 @@
         initial_configure = surface->current.serial == 0;
         surface->pending.serial = serial;
         surface->requested = surface->pending;
-        memset(&surface->pending, 0, sizeof(surface->pending));
+        /* A configure sequence without an xdg_toplevel.configure leaves the
+         * size and states of the toplevel as they were: a compositor may send
+         * one for a state this client does not know, for example when the
+         * window becomes hidden. Keep them for the next sequence, so that it
+         * is not taken for a request to leave the maximized state. */
+        surface->pending.serial = 0;
     }
 
     wayland_win_data_release(data);
